{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/704666-i-need-help-tying-the-party-together","id":704666,"title":"I need help tying the party together.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-17T04:56:20-07:00","id":704666,"title":"I need help tying the party together.","content":"Can anyone give me some tips on how to bring a party together? I'm going to be running a hunter game where the players are all residents on a creepy apartment/boarding house that used to be a creepy manor. The manor hides the body/spirit of a stryx that the local vampires have stuck into a kind of torpor because the stryx found a way tie itself to the Shadow so that if he dies/disrupted it will open up a verge. The party will spend the story arc dealing with hauntings &amp; normal &quot;monster of the week&quot; encounters culminating into a showdown with the fettered stryx. Hopefully they will do something bad, like killing it &amp; opening the Verge leading to other nasties","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T05:03:35-07:00","id":704686,"title":"","content":"Have all the PCs know a sweet old lady that bakes cookies and shit. Then kill her. They band together to investigate her highly suspicious death because the police are doing nothing about it and they all know something weird went down the night it happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T05:48:32-07:00","id":704724,"title":"","content":"Darn, I may use this but I was going to have a sweet old lady running the place I don't want her to die so soon... Maybe hospitalize her?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T06:47:29-07:00","id":704839,"title":"","content":"I guess that would work too.<br /> <br /> Basically anything that gives the player characters a common motive to stick their noses into the strange stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T01:23:13-07:00","id":708394,"title":"","content":"You could also have a large party for the inhabitants of the apartments. Perhaps one of the guests is a ghost, but nobody realizes it. The guest is friendly with the characters. Sometime later the person is found dead, and when the police arrives the corpse is gone and people learn that apartment 7b is uninhabited at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T15:08:40-07:00","id":724247,"title":"","content":"So, I'm going to start it with the mysterious owner of the manor is found dead with obvious occult signs &amp; ritualistic evidence. Hopefully that will be enough.<br /> <br /> My second problem is what to name the town. I was going to call it Greenville (most common town name in America) but now I'm thinking it should have a more creepy name, something with the vibe that something evil or powerful might have came to rest there. Some i have debated on...<br /> <br /> Starfall Hollow<br /> Godsfall<br /> Old One's Rest<br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> What sounds best? What are your own ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T15:23:59-07:00","id":724266,"title":"","content":"New Copse, except someone's vandalised the sign so that there's an r between the o and p.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T12:59:07-07:00","id":726805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aermas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/704666-i-need-help-tying-the-party-together#post704666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone give me some tips on how to bring a party together? I'm going to be running a hunter game where the players are all residents on a creepy apartment/boarding house that used to be a creepy manor. The manor hides the body/spirit of a stryx that the local vampires have stuck into a kind of torpor because the stryx found a way tie itself to the Shadow so that if he dies/disrupted it will open up a verge. The party will spend the story arc dealing with hauntings &amp; normal &quot;monster of the week&quot; encounters culminating into a showdown with the fettered stryx. Hopefully they will do something bad, like killing it &amp; opening the Verge leading to other nasties</div> </div> </div> </div>Flashbacks help alot.<br /> <br /> Basically allow the players to all encounter the monster previously and came to realize certain weaknesses and/or bans that it showed after that first escape.<br /> <br /> Encourage players to share this information with each other (and since it's the first session, fudge the dice when needed), and get them working with Tactics as a group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T12:10:20-08:00","id":760824,"title":"","content":"Okay, so here is what I've thought up so far...<br /> <br /> Their first archvillian is Braith Bracken, a Strix who was able to tie his form into the gauntlet, after the local vampires found him, they used a macguffin &quot;Sanguine Stake&quot; to pin his Shadow form to the corpse he was inhabitting, because they didn't know how to kill him without opening a Verge. Braith was able to find a loophole though. He used the Strix power to move into the twilight. He can't shift back until his body is freed of the stake &amp; so he has created a cult following of local teens &amp; troubled minds to free his body, which is under the manor.<br /> <br /> The game will open with the discovery of the manor owner dead, carved up by hooked knives &amp; blood trails leading out in the shape of feathered wings, &amp; bloody handprints on his head. Vampires are spooked &amp; get involved, the hunters hopefully start snooping &amp; band together. Does this seem alright?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T12:18:19-08:00","id":760833,"title":"","content":"Simplest way to tie a party together and make it stick? Make them do it for you. Just straight up ask your players: how do you know these other guys, what are your bonds and connections? How do you feel about them? What's your involvement with the supernatural, have you ever run into something that goes bump in the night before, maybe brushed it off at the time, but stuff that happens now might make you look back on it in a new light? Character generation isn't a solo act. Provide prompts, make sure they go in a direction that will be able to flow with the chronicle.<br /> <br /> As for town name, I'd say pick something unassuming and innocent, and use context to gradually imbue that innocent name with an undertone of dread. Oakville has a &quot;mystery spot&quot; tourist attraction here or there where things don't behave as they should. There's wilderness nearby that the locals quietly understand you should never go too deep into. Surveyors came by awhile back with evidence of a deep network of caverns underneath the town, but nobody in Oakville would sell the land so they could dig. Something's wrong in Oakville, and it's not just any one monster that's at cause over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 11-08-2015, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}